# Use data always (live-matched)

When choosing or defending entry, exit, stop, limits, pair sums, quiet gates, or any strategy default:

1. **Replay as live** — same gates and fill rules as the strategy defaults (quiet `|Δ|`, enter-after, no balanced fallback, hold stranded, scalp hold, etc.). Do not quote “all windows that printed cheap” as if it were the bot.
2. **Fills** — lift at the ask when the signal fires; the other leg fills only if a **later** ask reaches the rest price. Do not treat `lowest_*` alone as a both-fill.
3. **Show the table** (n, wins, losses, both-fills, EV, $) from that live-matched replay.
4. **Prefer hold-to-settle** unless the same live replay shows early exit wins.
5. If tick/snapshot data is too thin, say so — **do not invent defaults**.

Wrong: EV on every window with `lowest ≤ 20¢`, no quiet gate.
Right: walk ask + Δ snapshots; enter only when live gates pass; settle like the bot.
